<title>UK: Shell to award 650 mln stg North Sea contracts.</title>
<headline>Shell to award 650 mln stg North Sea contracts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell U.K. Exploration and Production, which operates in the North Sea on behalf of Royal Dutch/Shell and Exxon, said on Tuesday it planned to award service contracts worth 650 million sterling over the next seven years.</p>
<p>The contracts, which should be finalised within the next two to three months and take effect early in 1998, are planned for Wood Group Engineering, AMEC Process and Energy Ltd and a joint venture between Haliburton unit Brown and Root and Arabian Oil Co International, Shell said.</p>
</text>
